The attractions pod is crash-looping, and the frontend's calls to attractions are the only error spans in the data. I have enough to write up the root cause and its propagation path.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "attractions",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name='attractions-6cfc749b67-fc42d' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Attractions pod restart counter climbs from 2 to 6 during the incident, versus 0 in the normal period."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='attractions') AS spans_normal, (SELECT count(*) FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='attractions') AS spans_abnormal", "claim": "The attractions service emits 104 spans in the normal period and none during the incident."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT message, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE level='ERROR' GROUP BY message ORDER BY n DESC", "claim": "Frontend logs ERROR lines 'NearbyMus/NearbyCinema failed for hotelId', matching the failed attractions calls."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "attractions", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND (span_name LIKE 'HTTP /cinema%' OR span_name LIKE 'HTTP /museums%' OR span_name LIKE 'HTTP /restaurants%') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY n DESC", "claim": "Frontend HTTP /cinema, /museums and /restaurants return 500 with Error status, about 490 requests in total."}]}
  ]
}
```

